    a: "The most frequent JSON syntax errors are trailing commas after the last array item or object property, unquoted keys, single quotes instead of double quotes, and unescaped newline characters inside strings."
  - q: "Does this JSON formatter sort keys recursively?"
    a: "Yes. When 'Sort keys alphabetically' is enabled, keys are sorted in alphabetical order at the top level and inside all nested child objects."
  - q: "What is the maximum file size for formatting?"
    a: "For browser safety and smooth responsiveness, the tool enforces a client-side safety limit of 1 MB (1,048,576 characters). Large payloads are debounced to prevent interface lag."
  - q: "Is my JSON data uploaded to an external server?"
    a: "No. All formatting, key sorting, validation, and minification happen 100% locally in your browser memory. Your confidential API keys, payload dumps, and configuration files are never sent over the network."
  - q: "What is the difference between JSON formatting and minification?"
    a: "Formatting adds indentation and line breaks so human developers can easily inspect and debug data. Minification strips all unnecessary whitespace to minimize payload bandwidth for network transmissions."
